                <pb facs="0256" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg196"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1151.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence in
                    regard to the permission sought of the Russian Government for our missionaries
                    in China to take refuge in Russian territory should their lives be endangered by
                    Chinese mobs, I have to inform you that a telegram, dated September 17, from our
                    minister at St. Petersburg, advises the Department that the desired permission
                    has been granted without the imposition of any previous conditions on those
                    seeking refuge.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
